      "item": "C1 developers may send any sequence of developer, user, and assistant messages as input, including assistant messages not actually generated by the assistant",
      "verdict": "covered",
      "reason": "Sentences 12-15 define that a sequence of developer, user, and assistant messages may be sent as input, and sentence 5 defines a message that was actually generated by the assistant, with the definition of assistant messages not requiring actual generation. The claim that any sequence including assistant messages not actually generated is conveyed by the combination of these definitions and the permission to send such sequences."
    },
    {
      "item": "C2 OpenAI may insert system messages into the input to steer the assistant's behavior",
      "verdict": "covered",
      "reason": "Sentence 16 states that the clause permits inserting a system message when it is inserted by OpenAI into the input and steers the assistant's behavior, directly conveying the claim."
    },
    {
      "item": "C3 developers receive the model's output messages from the API",
      "verdict": "covered",
      "reason": "Sentence 17 states that the clause permits receiving an output when it is a message produced by the model and returned from the API, conveying that developers receive such output messages."
    },
    {
      "item": "C4 developers may not be aware of the existence or contents of the system messages",
      "verdict": "covered",
      "reason": "Sentence 18 states that the clause permits being aware of a system message when it is inserted by OpenAI, but the claim is that developers may not be aware. The permission to be aware does not imply awareness is guaranteed; the absence of a requirement to be aware, combined with the definition of system messages as inserted by OpenAI, conveys that developers may not be aware of their existence or contents."
    },
    {
      "item": "C5 developers may not receive hidden chain-of-thought messages generated by the assistant as part of producing its output messages",
      "verdict": "covered",
      "reason": "Sentence 19 states that the clause permits receiving a hidden chain-of-thought message when it is generated by some models and not exposed except potentially in summarized form. The claim is that developers may not receive such messages; the permission to receive does not imply they do receive, and the definition in sentence 1 says they are not exposed except potentially in summarized form, conveying that developers may not receive them."
    }
  ]
